---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import JoinBand from '../components/JoinBand.astro';
import { SITE, LINKS } from '../data/site';

const neuroFormats = [
  { t: 'Labs', d: 'Short experiments you run on yourself, like reaction time, the Stroop test, and memory span. Then we look at the class results together.' },
  { t: 'Guest speakers', d: 'People who work in medicine and brain science. You bring the questions.' },
  { t: 'Journal club', d: 'One published paper, broken down into what they asked, what they did, and what they found.' },
  { t: 'Ethics debates', d: 'An open question in neuroscience, with sides assigned at random.' },
  { t: 'Brain Bee prep', d: 'High-yield topics and timed practice for the Brain Bee competition.' },
  { t: 'Brain Awareness Week', d: 'In March we take quick brain science demos to the rest of the school.' },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="How NeuroGIDAS works: alternating neuroscience and GIDAS research weeks, what GIDAS and miRcore are, and who the club is for.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="h1">A brain science club and a research lab, sharing one room.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        NeuroGIDAS brings two things together that usually live in separate clubs: how the brain works, and hands-on genetics
        research with the same databases scientists use.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2 class="h2">How the weeks work</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We meet every Wednesday after school. One week is neuroscience, the next is GIDAS research, and the year runs on both
          tracks at once. Come to both, or just the one you care about.
        </p>
        <p>
          The two tracks meet in the middle. Cancer is this year’s research focus across the GIDAS network, so later in the year
          we spend time on brain cancer, where the biology of the brain and the genetics of disease overlap.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top track-sec" style="--c: var(--neuro)">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2 class="h2">Neuroscience weeks</h2>
        <p class="track-sub">The part you can see and do.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="prose">
          We cover how the brain is built and how it works: neurons and how signals travel, memory, perception, sleep, and what
          happens when things go wrong. Most meetings pair a short lesson with something you actually do.
        </p>
        <dl class="formats">
          {
            neuroFormats.map((f) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{f.t}</dt>
                <dd>{f.d}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top track-sec" style="--c: var(--gidas)">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2 class="h2">GIDAS weeks</h2>
        <p class="track-sub">Research on public data.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>GIDAS stands for Genes in Diseases and Symptoms.</strong> It is the high school program of{' '}
          <a href={LINKS.mircore} rel="noopener">miRcore</a>, a nonprofit affiliated with the University of Michigan, with more than
          130 chapters.
        </p>
        <p>
          You start with the basics, like DNA and the central dogma. Then you move on to the research tools: NCBI GEO and GEO2R to pull
          and analyze gene expression data, STRING to map how proteins interact, KEGG to find shared pathways, and GeneCards,
          OMIM, Gene Ontology, and the UCSC Genome Browser to understand the genes you find.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each member builds one project across the whole year. It ends with a written abstract and a presentation at the miRcore
          High School Research Conference in April.
        </p>
        <p><a class="link" href="/research/">See the research path step by step</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2 class="h2">Who it is for</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Anyone at Eastview. No experience needed.</strong> You might have taken AP Biology, written some code, or done
          neither. The first meetings are there to put everyone on the same footing.
        </p>
        <p>
          It helps most if you are curious about medicine, neuroscience, genetics, bioinformatics, or research in general. Not
          many high schoolers get to finish a year with their own research question, data they analyzed themselves, and an abstract with their name on
          it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2 class="h2">When and where</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Day</dt><dd>{SITE.day}, after school</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Time</dt><dd class="tnum">{SITE.time}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Room</dt><dd>{SITE.room}, {SITE.advisor}’s room</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Run by</dt><dd>Co-presidents Aaryav Sharma and Rishik Kondadadi</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <JoinBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: var(--s-6) clamp(2rem, 1rem + 5vw, 6rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .track-sec .h2 {
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--c);
  }

  .track-sub {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .formats {
    margin: var(--s-7) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0 var(--s-6);
  }

  .formats div {
    padding: var(--s-4) 0 var(--s-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }

  .formats dt {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 106;
  }

  .formats dd {
    margin: var(--s-1) 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .facts {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }

  .facts div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s-4);
    padding: var(--s-4) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .facts dt {
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .formats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .facts div {
      grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
